QuestGuidance.Register("en",345,{
[11009]="7002F92F\n1\tTalk to Trumsele the silversmith about Odwacer's order\tTrumsele can be found at the merchant's area in Cliving, just west of the fountain. Ordwacer has asked you to demand the purchased items from Trumsele, or he will be forced to deal with the town guard.\n2\tTalk to the quartermaster about the shipment of mouldings\tThe quartermaster of Cliving can be found south of the fountain, not far from the main entrance to the city. Trumsele has requested that you inquire with the quartermaster as to when the arrival of the mouldings being transported to Cliving from Edoras is to be expected.\n3\tTalk to Trumsele about what to do next\tTrumsele can be found at the merchant's area in Cliving, just west of the fountain. The quartermaster has informed you that the delivery is not to be expected anytime soon. Trumsele will need to find another way to appease his client.\n4\tTalk to Ordwacer\tOrdwacer can be found at his estate east of the central fountain in Cliving. Trumsele has asked you to offer Ordwacer the ability to negotiate bargains with him, in exchange for his tolerance of the unfulfilled order.\n",
[11010]="7000012A\n1\tBring the nestadalas-fronds to Bolli\030Collect nestadalas-fronds (total: 4)\tNestedelais can be found to the north-east of Frerin's Court. Bolli mentioned that the leaves of the nestadalas-bush were necessary for his cure and asked you to gather some fronds for him.\n",
[11011]="70068369\n1\tCollect wild hog hides ([see journal]/10)\tYou will find wild hogs throughout the crags and moors of the eastern Cape of Umbar. Kill them and collect their hides for Abido.\n2\tYou will find wild hogs throughout the crags and moors of the eastern Cape of Umbar. Kill them and collect their hides for Abido.\t\n",
[11012]="700681CE\n1\tInvestigate suspicious areas in the marsh\tHeshra has asked you to investigate the marsh east of Khûtra near the shore for anything unusual.\n2\tReturn to Heshra, the herbalist\tReturn to the herbalist Heshra in the Elder Hall.\n",
[11013]="700681D5\n1\tReturn to Heshra, the herbalist\030Collect milk thistles ([see journal]/10)\030Collect nasturtiums ([see journal]/8)\030Collect sprigwort ([see journal]/6)\tHeshra, the herbalist, has asked you to collect various herbs for a simple salve to treat the disease. These herbs can be found in the hills north of Khûtra.\n2\tAdminister the simple salve to the afflicted villagers. They can be found on the rocks just outside Khûtra, to the east near the shore.\t\n3\tReturn to Heshra, the herbalist\tReturn to Heshra the herbalist in the Elder Hall.\n",
[11014]="700681E2\n1\tTalk to Ziriha the merchant and acquire rare ingredients\tSpeak with Ziriha the merchant about the rare ingredients Heshra needs. She can be found near the fishing pier.\n2\tReturn to Heshra with the ingredients\030Harvest sponge mushrooms ([see journal]/6)\tHarvest sponge mushrooms that grow in the hills east of Khûtra.\n3\tAdminister first experimental salve to diseased goat\030Administer second experimental salve to a diseased goat\030Administer third experimental salve to a diseased goat\tAdminister the new salves to afflicted goats. They can be found outside the Elder Hall.\n4\tReturn to Heshra, the herbalist\tReturn to Heshra the herbalist in the Elder Hall\n",
[11015]="700191A9\n1\tTalk to Orthir\tOrthir can be found a short distance west of Cerin Amroth, near the path. Mallendathor wishes you to speak to Orthir, the Scholar of the Trees, to see if he knows what might heal the saplings' malady.\n2\tSing to a Malbrethil-sapling (0/4)\tThe Malbrethil-saplings can be found around Cerin Brethil in Taur Hith, to the north-east of Cerin Amroth. Orthir believes that the saplings, deprived of the everyday music of the now-wary forest, might be revived if you were to sing to them.\n3\tSing to a Malbrethil-sapling (1/4)\tThe Malbrethil-saplings can be found around Cerin Brethil in Taur Hith, to the north-east of Cerin Amroth. Orthir believes that the saplings, deprived of the everyday music of the now-wary forest, might be revived if you were to sing to them.\n4\tSing to a Malbrethil-sapling (2/4)\tThe Malbrethil-saplings can be found around Cerin Brethil in Taur Hith, to the north-east of Cerin Amroth. Orthir believes that the saplings, deprived of the everyday music of the now-wary forest, might be revived if you were to sing to them.\n5\tSing to a Malbrethil-sapling (3/4)\tThe Malbrethil-saplings can be found around Cerin Brethil in Taur Hith, to the north-east of Cerin Amroth. Orthir believes that the saplings, deprived of the everyday music of the now-wary forest, might be revived if you were to sing to them.\n6\tCollect Malbrethil-seeds (total: 6)\tMallendathor has asked you to gather Malbrethil-seeds from in the area of Taur Hith, to the north-east of Cerin Amroth. The seeds are difficult to find, but are frequently collected by the hungry shrews that scamper about the forest there.\n7\tTalk to Sendiel in Gelirdor\tSendiel is in Gelirdor, south-west of the Malbrethil-trees, east of Cerin Amroth. Orthir instructed you to tell Sendiel of your success.\n",
[11016]="70040CF1\n1\tDestroy sinister-looking barrels (total: 8)\tSinister-looking barrels are scattered around Abedec's Watch in southern Belfalas. You should destroy the sinister-looking barrels.\n2\tCompleted\tYou have destroyed the explosives brought ashore by Abedec's Corsairs. They were surely intended to bring down the old stone walls of Gondor's ancient cities.\n",
[11017]="70042901\n1\tTalk to Bingo in the Golden Perch Inn and travel with him to practice swimming\tBingo is in the Golden Perch Inn, in the town of Stock. He is waiting for you to speak with him when you are ready to practice the art of swimming.\n2\tTalk to Bingo Boffin inside the Golden Perch Inn, in the town of Stock\tBingo is in the Golden Perch Inn, in the town of Stock.\n",
[11018]="7003FDE1\n1\tDestroy boats (total: 9)\tThe small boats the corsairs used should be destroyed.\n",
[11019]="70067C3B\n1\tChallenge Rûnax in the hills of the Cape of Umbar West\030Challenge Shâba in the hills near Jax Phanâl\tHead into the wilds of the western Cape of Umbar. Search the plains, hills, and mountain edges for the goat sire and dam. Weaken them and use the toxin on them docile. When you've captured both goats, deliver them to Stúkha at the crest of Jax Phanâl.\n2\tDeliver the pair of goats to Stúkha at the crest of Jax Phanâl\tYou've captured both goats. Deliver them to Stúkha at the crest of Jax Phanâl. NOTE: The rams will find their way if you become separated.\n",
[11020]="7004148E\n1\tTalk to Roamingstar\tRoamingstar can be found in her glade in north-eastern Dor-en-Ernil. Roamingstar has agreed to aid you in preventing the Ruthless Dead from crossing into Lebennin. You should speak to her when you are ready.\n2\tTalk to Roamingstar\tRoamingstar can be found in her glade in north-eastern Dor-en-Ernil. You have aided Roamingstar in banishing the Ruthless Dead and should now speak to her.\n3\tTalk to Garvir in Linhir\tGarvir can be found in Linhir in eastern Dor-en-Ernil. You have prevented the Ruthless Dead from crossing into Lebennin and should return to Garvir to tell him of your deeds with Roamingstar.\n",
[11021]="70010795\n1\tCatch as many fish as you can in twenty minutes\tThe docks are at Celondim in Ered Luin, far to the west of Bree and the Shire. The docks of Celondim have long been a popular site for Elven Fishermen. They have allowed you some time to catch fish for the hobbits' Lithe Festival.\n",
[11022]="7006B6C6\n1\tTalk to Girhâzi in Iridír\tNingêna has asked you to return to Girhâzi and update her on the situation at Sûru.\n",
[11023]="7001751B\n1\tDefeat the Lost One\tThe Lost One is below the Sixteenth Hall, south-east of the Twenty-first Hall. You have been challenged to prove your great worth by defeating the Lost One without making the battle easier by killing his summoned gredbyg.\n2\tReturn to Sigurd at the Twenty-first Hall\tThe dwarf Sigurd can be found in the Twenty-first Hall, north-west of the Sixteenth Hall. Sigurd will be very impressed to hear that you met his challenge of defeating the Lost One while the gredbyg harried your efforts all the while.\n",
[11024]="70017520\n1\tDefeat enemies in the Sixteenth Hall (total: 100)\tGlobsnaga spread their poison in the Sixteenth Hall, south-east of the Twenty-first Hall whence you came. You have been asked to slay as many Globsnaga as you can to ensure the safety of the dwarves in Moria.\n2\tReturn to Geirr at the Twenty-first Hall\tGeirr is in the Twenty-first Hall, north-west of the Sixteenth Hall. You should return to Geirr and tell him of your success against the Globsnaga, for he wishes to see if you are as sturdy a warrior as rumour has assured.\n",
[11025]="70017513\n1\tReturn the hide to Eilíefr at the Twenty-first Hall\030Collect the The Lost One's hide (quantity: see journal)\tThe Lost One is below the Sixteenth Hall, south-east of the Twenty-first Hall where Eilíefr stands. You have been challenged to prove your great worth by defeating the Lost One and returning with its hide as a trophy of your victory.\n",
[11026]="7005F6B7\n1\tDefeat maddened ukhrâsh at Skelstrand\tMaddened ukhrâsh can be found along the banks of Durthuzâram at Skelstrand in Gloomingtarn. Disturbed by the arrival of the Iron Crown and Orcs in Gloomingtarn, maddened ukhrâsh have swelled onto the banks of Durthuzâram at Skelstrand. You should defeat the maddened ukhrâsh at Skelstrand.\n2\tDefeat maddened ukhrâsh at Skelstrand (total: 8)\tMaddened ukhrâsh can be found along the banks of Durthuzâram at Skelstrand in Gloomingtarn. Disturbed by the arrival of the Iron Crown and Orcs in Gloomingtarn, maddened ukhrâsh have swelled onto the banks of Durthuzâram at Skelstrand. You should defeat the maddened ukhrâsh at Skelstrand.\n3\tCompleted\tYou have defeated many of the maddened ukhrâsh at Skelstrand and driven them back into Durthuzâram.\n",
[11027]="700195BF\n1\tDefeat marsh-flies (total: 8)\tMarsh-flies can be found near the lake east of Archet. Fenton Marshley has asked you to hunt down the marsh-flies that plague Archet.\n2\tTalk to Fenton Marshley at the Hunter's Lodge\tFenton Marshley is near the Hunter's Lodge, east of Archet. You should return to Fenton Marshley for your reward.\n",
[11028]="700001B5\n1\tBring the Warg-hides to Odbjórn\030Collect white Warg-hide\030Collect rugged Warg-hides (total: 5)\tWargs can be found at Urugarth, west of Tármunn Súrsa. Odbjorn is at Tármunn Súrsa. Odbjórn requires Warg hides to craft new armour for the resistance. You should take several hides, as well as the hide of the Warg-leader, and return them to Odbjórn.\n",
[11029]="700000C9\n1\tSpeak with Strider to skip the Introduction\tIf you would like to skip the remainder of the introductory tutorial experience and be transported to Archet following the burning of the town, speak with Strider.\n",
[11030]="70000133\n1\tTalk to Bounder Boffin to skip the Introduction\tIf you would like to skip the remainder of the introductory tutorial experience and be transported to Little Delving in the Shire following the burning of the town of Archet, speak with Bounder Boffin.\n",
[11031]="70001064\n1\tTalk to Elrond to skip the Introduction\tIf you would like to skip the remainder of the introductory tutorial experience and be transported to Falathlorn following the defeat of the Dourhands, speak with Elrond.\n",
[11032]="70002E79\n1\tTalk to Gandalf to skip the Introduction\tIf you would like to skip the remainder of the introductory tutorial experience and be transported to Thorin's Gate following the defeat the Dourhands, speak with Gandalf.\n",
[11033]="7001EE4F\n1\tTalk to Nos Grimsong to skip the Introduction\tIf you would like to skip the remainder of the introductory tutorial experience and be transported to Falathlorn following the defeat of the Dourhands, speak with Nos Grimsong.\n",
[11034]="7001EE50\n1\tTalk to Celandine Brandybuck to skip the Introduction\tIf you would like to skip the remainder of the introductory tutorial experience and be transported to Little Delving in the Shire following the burning of the town of Archet, speak with Celandine Brandybuck.\n",
[11035]="7001EE51\n1\tTalk to Celandine Brandybuck to skip the Introduction\tIf you would like to skip the remainder of the introductory tutorial experience and be transported to Archet following the burning of the town, speak with Celandine Brandybuck.\n",
[11036]="7001EE52\n1\tTalk to Nos Grimsong to skip the Introduction\tIf you would like to skip the remainder of the introductory tutorial experience and be transported to Thorin's Gate following the defeat of the Dourhands, speak with Nos Grimsong.\n",
[11037]="7003A48E\n1\tSpeak with Kehleyr to bypass the Introduction\tIf you would like to skip the remainder of the introductory tutorial experience, speak with Kehleyr again.\n",
[11038]="70041F2A\n1\tTalk to Celandine Brandybuck to skip the Introduction\tIf you would like to skip the remainder of the introductory tutorial experience and be transported to Archet following the burning of the town, speak with Celandine Brandybuck.\n",
[11039]="7004B9F1\n1\tSpeak with Harthalín to skip the Introduction\tIf you would like to skip the remainder of the introduction and be transported to Celondim, speak with Harthalín.\n",
[11040]="7004B9F3\n1\tSpeak with Sterkist beside Grimbeorn's pond to skip the Introduction\tIf you would like to skip the remainder of the introduction and be transported to Archet, speak with Sterkist.\n",
